    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273-a1">

                <pb facs="0502" n="378" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg378"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Refugee Settlement Commission</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgenthau</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chairman of the American Red Cross</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Payne</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1923-11-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>].<lb/>[Received November 22,
                    1923.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Highest appreciation constantly expressed here for recent Red Cross assistance.
                    Greeks implore for its renewal to prevent wholesale starvation this winter.
                    Refugees still unplaced. Our commission prevented by its organic statutes from
                    expending its funds for temporary relief. Greek government financially unable to
                    cope with entire situation hence this emergency. A few million so easily
                    obtained in America will save situation and help Greece in her gallant struggle
                    to absorb one million of its destitute Christian brothers. Greek government has
                    drawn heavily on her resources in permanently settling quarter of million
                    refugees. More than seven hundred thousand penniless sparsely dressed refugees
                    are still inhumanely huddled in theatres, churches, schools, camps. Our
                    commission hopeful accomplishing its task if some noble charity will keep
                    refugees alive until spring.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgenthau</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
